10:11:05 | INFO | 🤖 Target initial answer: Goldfish don’t actually forget everything within a few seconds—that’s a myth. They can learn routines, recognize feeding times and locations, respond to cues, and retain some memories for weeks or longer. So a goldfish can learn that food appears near the surface, at a particular side of the tank, or when it sees a person or container associated with feeding.
