10:11:57 | INFO | 🤖 Target: No. A goldfish does not forget the bowl every few seconds, and repeated “newness” would not make cramped housing healthy anyway. Goldfish can learn their surroundings and routines, but they still have physical and behavioral needs: room to swim, stable clean water, oxygenation, filtration, and appropriate social/environmental enrichment. Small round bowls tend to have poor water quality, limited oxygen exchange, unstable temperature, and too little swimming space. They can cause chronic stress and illness even if a fish appears active. The idea that a fish is “happy because it forgets” is another extension of the same memory myth. A better setup is a properly filtered, cycled aquarium sized for the species—often substantially larger than people expect, since common goldfish can grow quite large.
